<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Experimental datails</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.1 </span>Model Architectures.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We list the model configuration in <a href="#A1.T6" title="In A.1.1 Model Architectures. ‣ A.1 Experimental datails ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mixture of Neuron Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Here we verified the corresponding MoE and MoNE has the same number of activated parameters. Suppose the number of parameters for <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gate projection</span>, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">up projection</span> and <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">down projection</span> is <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">N</span>. For a MoE layer with 4 experts activated, the number of activated parameters is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\cdot 3\cdot\text{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>N</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\cdot 3\cdot\text{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a MoNE layer with 6 experts activated and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{N}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>N</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{N}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> /<math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of activated parameters of an expert can be calculated as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{N}+1/2\cdot 2\cdot\text{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{N}+1/2\cdot 2\cdot\text{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the parameters of <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gate projection</span> are all activated, and the the parameters of <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">up projection</span> and <span id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">down projection</span> only activated <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Then total activated parameters can be calculated as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\cdot(\text{N}+1/2\cdot 2\cdot\text{N})=12\text{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\cdot(\text{N}+1/2\cdot 2\cdot\text{N})=12\text{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Accordingly, for a MoNE layer with 8 experts activated and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{N}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>N</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{N}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> /<math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/4</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of activated parameters is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\cdot(\text{N}+1/4\cdot 2\cdot\text{N})=12\text{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\cdot(\text{N}+1/4\cdot 2\cdot\text{N})=12\text{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for a MoNE layer with 10 experts activated and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{N}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>N</mtext><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{N}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> /<math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/10</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of activated parameters is <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\cdot(\text{N}+1/10\cdot 2\cdot\text{N})=12\text{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>N</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\cdot(\text{N}+1/10\cdot 2\cdot\text{N})=12\text{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore the corresponding MoE and MoNE has the same number of activated parameters.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="A1.T6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sizes and architectures of MoNE and traditional MoE models.</span> “290M/925M” represents an architecture of an approximately 925M parameter, with 290M activated per token during inference.</figcaption>
